# SmartDNS force-foreign.conf
# Purpose: per-domain DNS overrides. Two distinct problems live here.
#
#   1. VPN exit IP triggers a server-side redirect loop -> pin to a CN IP
#      with `address`, so the request takes the direct path (Bing, below).
#   2. The domestic resolver returns a wrong answer -> route the lookup to
#      the foreign group with `nameserver` (models.dev, below).
#
# These pull in opposite directions. Check which one you have before adding
# a line: resolve the domain against two encrypted sources and compare. If
# they agree, the DNS is fine and the problem is the exit IP.
#
# DIAGNOSIS METHOD (Playwright redirect capture):
#   1. Capture redirect chain in browser
#   2. Identify the loop pattern
#   3. Check if CN IP direct access serves content (no redirect back)
#   4. Add address override if CN IP is in bypass_ipv4 AND serves content directly
#
# Microsoft Bing: ERR_TOO_MANY_REDIRECTS
#   Root cause (confirmed by Exa research + Playwright capture):
#   - Microsoft detects commercial VPN exit IPs as "China VPN users"
#   - www.bing.com (VPN IP) -> 302 -> cn.bing.com
#   - cn.bing.com (VPN IP, global edge) -> 301 -> www.bing.com?mkt=zh-CN -> loop
#   Fix: force BOTH to 202.89.233.101 (CN bypass IP, DIRECT path).
#   With CN ISP IP: www.bing.com -> cn.bing.com (1 redirect) -> serves content.
#   TLS verified: cert at 202.89.233.101 has SAN *.bing.com + www.bing.com.
#   Reference: Clash Verge #1702, SearxNG #2193, V2EX t/927161
address /bing.com/202.89.233.101
address /cn.bing.com/202.89.233.101

# models.dev: the domestic resolver hands back the wrong host
#   alidns  DoH -> 67.15.129.210 (theplanet.com), TTL 15
#   doh.pub DoH -> 104.26.8.108, 172.67.69.147, ... (Cloudflare), TTL 300
#   Both queries are encrypted, so this is not injection on the wire -- the
#   two upstreams genuinely disagree and the domestic group answers first.
#   Cloudflare is right: models.dev runs on alex/elle.ns.cloudflare.com.
#   Port 443 on the wrong host does answer, which is why this reads as
#   ERR_CERT_COMMON_NAME_INVALID in a browser and as a handshake timeout to
#   curl, rather than as a connection refused.
# Routing the domain through the proxy does NOT fix this. The address is
#   already wrong by the time sing-box sees it.
nameserver /models.dev/foreign
